      "taskType": "application",
      "prompt": "Simplify $({{a}}+{{b}}i)({{a}}-{{b}}i)-{{c}}$. This expression combines complex multiplication and subtraction. Show the conjugate product, then write the final result in standard complex form.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "conjugate-product",
          "label": "Value of the conjugate product",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{product}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "real-part",
          "label": "Final real part after subtracting {{c}}",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "{{re}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "imag-coefficient",
          "label": "Final imaginary coefficient",
          "inputProfile": "number",
          "expected": "0"
        },
        {
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Final complex number",
          "inputProfile": "expression",
          "expected": "{{re}}+0*i"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Conjugates multiply to a real number.",
        "reasoning": [
          "({{a}}+{{b}}i)({{a}}-{{b}}i)={{a}}^2+{{b}}^2={{product}} because i²=-1.",
          "Subtract {{c}} to get {{re}}.",
          "The imaginary component is 0, so the final result is purely real."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "${{re}}$"
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Do the conjugate multiplication first; the imaginary cross-terms cancel."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Use (a+bi)(a-bi)=a²+b²."
      ],
